---
import './memory.css';
---
<figure class="memory-figure">
 <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 3</span>An expiry time is not a reservation</div>
 <div class="scene">
  <div class="expiry-start box"><strong>0 seconds: insert P7</strong>Expiry deadline: 30 seconds after insertion.</div>
  <div class="expiry-paths">
   <div><p><strong>Memory pressure</strong></p><div class="box"><strong>10 s · evicted</strong>Its space is reused for another answer.</div><div class="down" aria-hidden="true">↓</div><div class="box"><strong>12 s · P7 misses</strong>Read the source, although the original expiry time has not arrived.</div></div>
   <div><p><strong>No earlier removal</strong></p><div class="box"><strong>12 s · P7 hits</strong>The copy is still resident and usable.</div><div class="down" aria-hidden="true">↓</div><div class="box"><strong>30 s · expires</strong>The copy must no longer be returned, even if its storage awaits cleanup.</div></div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <figcaption>Two invented histories of the same inserted copy. Both have a 30-second insertion TTL. No update or invalidation occurs, and the drawing stops following a copy once it is removed. A later refill would have its own lifetime.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
 .expiry-start { text-align:center; }.expiry-paths { display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem; }.down { text-align:center;font-size:1.4rem; }
 @media(max-width:540px){.expiry-paths{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.4rem;}}
</style>
